            "bug_id": 19257,
            "text": "Created attachment 3961\nset parent of internal environments to baseenv()\n\nCurrently, a number of environments associated with S4 methods are given assigned parents imprudently. This generates a _very_ substantial overhead on lazy-load and very noticeable .rdb file size bloat because serializing environments in general requires walking all parents.\n\nFor example, Bug #19239 found that `loadNamespace()` for these 5 packages takes about 18s:\n\n```\nfor (pkg in c(\"Gviz\", \"ShortRead\", \"raster\", \"timeSeries\", \"MatrixExtra\")) loadNamespace(pkg)\n```\n\nThe patch here reduces that by >30% to 11s, and reduces the total .rdb size of the 50 loaded S4 packages by 20MiB (45%).\n\nThe change is safe (as tested against several 100 packages) because the parent of these environments is never read in the first place -- `inherits=FALSE` is always used (or it's accesses by `names()`/`as.list()`/other accessors that don't walk the parents):\n\n- methods/R/methodsTable.R:261-285:\n   + Line 268: `exists(label, envir = table, inherits = FALSE)`\n   + Line 303: `get(label, envir = table)` (guarded by line 268).\n- methods/R/methodsTable.R:1318-1324:\n   + Removes the `.__T__` binding from `where`: `if (exists(tname, where, inherits = FALSE)) rm(list = tname, pos = where)`.\n- methods/R/methodsTable.R:1337-1369:\n   + Line 1342: `get(.TableMetaName(...), envir = as.environment(where), inherits = FALSE)`.\n   + Line 1352: `get(.TableMetaName(...), envir = as.environment(where), inherits = FALSE)`.\n- methods/R/methodsTable.R:1379-1402:\n   + Line 1397: `if (exists(label, envir = table, inherits = FALSE)).\n- methods/R/methodsTable.R:1460-1474:\n   + `get0(what, envir = where, inherits = FALSE)`.\n\nThe approach of setting `baseenv()` as parent is also used elsewhere in {methods} already, e.g. in `.classTable`, `.genericTable`, and `.implicitTable`.\n\nNB: This change requires rebuilding each package to re-generate the .rdb and get the benefits, so it makes sense to target it for the next major R release (e.g. R 4.7.0)."
          }
        ]
